# Docker environment

- Stay on Debian Bookworm Slim as the final base image.
- Keep the multi-stage build (Node, Go, Rust, uv tool stages).
- Keep a non-root runtime user (`developer`).
- Put container files under `docker/rootfs/` (paths match the image).
- Default interactive shell is **zsh** (skel under `etc/skel/.zshrc*`); tmux under `etc/tmux/`.
- Never copy SSH keys or tokens into the image.
- Preserve BuildKit cache mounts for APT where used.
- Install APT packages with `--no-install-recommends`.
- Clean APT lists after installs (`rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*`).
- Prefer changes that work on both `amd64` and `arm64`.
- Do not grow the image without a clear need.
- Keep Docker socket out of the base Compose file; add it only via `docker-compose.docker.yml`.
- After Dockerfile or Compose edits, validate with `make validate` and `make build` when Docker is available.
